oose methods based on place value, quantity and accurate working, rather than guessing digits by shape alone. Keep every step justified.\n\nHOW TO WORK\nRead the worked example and name the places, values or distances that carry the method. Before looking at the correction, make your own attempt using the exact question provided. Compare your working with the feedback: did you use the same skill and show your reasoning? If a digit or place is uncertain, identify what would have to be regrouped or counted again. One deliberate, justified revision is more useful than writing a longer answer.","icon":"📖","notice":"Repeating the worked example cannot show transfer to new numbers. Correct the value or method, not just the appearance of the digits.","title":"Transfer to a new problem"}],"title":"Year 3, Week 10, Lesson 3: Multiplication word problems","unit_number":3,"unit_title":"Multiplication and division","week":10,"week_in_unit":2,"word_challenges":null,"worked_example":"WORK THROUGH THIS\n4 bags with 6 apples each → 4×6=24 apples. An array of 5 rows of 3 seats → 5×3=15 seats.\n\nWrite what makes this example accurate, naming the places, values or distances used.","worked_visuals":[{"alt":"Equal-groups story matched to multiplication.","caption":"Factors match groups and group size.","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 660 150\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fff4ea\" stroke=\"#b87445\"/><rect x=\"340\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#e8f5ed\" stroke=\"#297a61\"/><g font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#263948\"><text x=\"28\" y=\"42\">Groups</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"78\">4 bags of 6</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"42\">Product</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"78\">24</text></g></svg>"},{"alt":"Array story contrasted with a wrong addition.","caption":"Structure decides the expression.","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 660 150\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\